WHERE THE DATA COMES FROM
-------------------------
Telemetry is accessed through FastF1 (https://github.com/theOehrly/Fast-F1),
an open-source Python library that reads Formula 1's publicly available timing
and telemetry feed. This project does not redistribute FastF1, does not proxy
the feed, and does not operate any service that serves F1 data to third
parties. All fetching happens on a developer's own machine, deliberately, by
running `pipeline/build_replay.py`; the deployed web application never contacts
the timing feed.


THE GALLERY FILES
-----------------
`app/public/gallery/` contains three curated historical excerpts, committed so
the deployed site has something to show without a backend:

  silverstone-2024-rain.json      2024 British Grand Prix, race, laps 24-28
  silverstone-2024-finale.json    2024 British Grand Prix, race, laps 48-52
  monza-2024-pit-cycle.json       2024 Italian Grand Prix, race, laps 13-19

Each is a small, transformed excerpt of a past session — three cars over a few
laps, resampled onto a 10 Hz grid — not a reproduction of the source feed. They
exist to demonstrate the software. They are limited in number and length on
purpose, and the project does not offer, and will not add, on-demand access to
arbitrary sessions.

